From ccfc8fc4e8daf367189488e437a55274d6c338f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ttabouch12 <ttabouch12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:10:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/21] extcon: sm5705: add Silicon Mitus SM5705 MUIC driver

The SM5705 companion chip of Exynos7870 Samsung devices has a MUIC whose
register map is not compatible with the SM5502/SM5504 (extra INT3/INTMASK3
pair, device-type registers elsewhere), so add a dedicated driver.

The driver switches the MUIC to manual mode, routes D+/D- to the USB
controller and reports USB / USB host / SDP / CDP / DCP / slow charger
cables through extcon. Add the matching devicetree binding.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C7LhHWjrzX28CzyNMEnVDk
